  "query_preview": "..\n\nToday through Sunday...\n\nSeasonably warm conditions under mostly sunny to sunny skies \nexist today as a ridge of high pressure over the central United \nStates nudges into the region. Over the plains of eastern Montana \n(generally around and east of Rosebud County), windy conditions \nexist today as well, with peak wind gusts in the 20s to lower 40s \n(mph). This evening into tonight, expected these winds to \ngradually subside. Low temperatures tonight will be in the 30s and\n40s (F) for most. \n\nTuesday into Thursday will remain seasonably warm with high \ntemperatures mainly in the 60s and 70s (F), warmest on Thursday. \nLow temperatures during this time will be in the 30s to lower 50s \nas well, coldest Tuesday night behind a dry cold front passage on \nTuesday. Through this time, mainly dry conditions are forecast, \nthough there is an occasional slight chance of precipitation over \nthe Absaroka-Beartooth mountains. Late Thursday into Friday, winds\nbegin to increase over the Bighorn mountains ahead of the next \nweather system. With this, southwesterly wind gusts in the 30s to \n50 mph are forecast. While the strongest winds look to remain in \nthe mountains during this time, windy conditions may spread over \nthe plains around and south/east of Buffalo, WY. With this, a few \nstronger gusts could impact far south and eastern Sheridan County,\nWyoming Friday ahead of the cold front (medium chance). \n\nFriday into Saturday, a weather system will likely bring cooler \ntemperatures, windy conditions, and precipitation to the area. \nWhile uncertainty remains regarding the exact evolution of the \nweather system through our region, the most likely scenario at \nthis point looks to be a strong cold front passage with scattered \nprecipitation as a low pressure system to the south merges with a \ntrough passing to the north. As far as the wind potential goes, \nthere is currently a medium chance of seeing wind gusts greater \nthan 40 mph across the region late Friday into Saturday morning. \nWhile the chance is lower, there could even be a few 50 mph wind \ngusts around Wheatland County (MT) and Sheridan County (WY). For \nprecipitation potential, the chance of precipitation is greatest \nover south-central/western Montana and north-western/central \nWyoming (70+ percent chance of precipitation). Cannot rule out a \nweak thunderstorm or two as well, though the chance is low (10 \npercent). While all rain is forecast over the plains during this \nevent, snow levels starting around 10,000 feet look to drop to \naround 5,000 feet Saturday. Therefore, snow is anticipated in the \nmountains during this event. As far as amounts go, the chance of \nseeing 0.50 inches of liquid precipitation (rain or melted snow) \nis 50 to 80 percent over south-central Montana, decreasing well \nbelow 50 percent over eastern Montana. The chance of seeing 6 or \nmore inches of snow is 50 percent in the Absaroka-Beartooth \nmountains and lower in the surrounding mountain ranges.\n\nConditions trend drier later Saturday into Sunday as a ridge of \nhigh pressure builds back over the region. LA",
